 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Formas",
    "@en": "Forms"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**I have** / **you have** / **we have** / **they have** + participio: **I have been** (he estado). **She has been** (ha estado).",
     "@en": "**I have** / **you have** / **we have** / **they have** + participle: **I have been** (I've been). **She has been** (has been)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "El participio de los verbos regulares es igual que el pasado: **walk** → **walked**, **play** → **played**.",
     "@en": "The participle of regular verbs is the same as the past: **walk** → **walked**, **play** → **played**."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Participios irregulares",
    "@en": "Irregular species"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**Be** → **been** (sido, estado). **Go** → **gone** (ido). **See** → **seen** (visto). **Eat** → **eaten** (comido). **Write** → **written** (escrito).",
     "@en": "**Be** → **been** (been, status). **Go** → **gone** (gone). **See** → **seen** (seen) **Eat** → **eaten** (eaten). **Write** → **written** (written)"
    },
    {
     "@es": "Algunos son iguales al pasado (**have** → **had**), pero muchos no: **see** → **saw** (pasado) / **seen** (participio).",
     "@en": "Some are equal to the past (**have** → **had**), but many are not: **see** → **saw** (past) / **seen** (participle)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Cuándo se usa",
    "@en": "When used"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Para experiencias sin fecha: **I have been to Italy** (he estado en Italia). Si dices cuándo fue, usa el pasado simple: **I was in Italy in 2019**.",
     "@en": "For undated experiences: **I have been to Italy** (I have been in Italy). If you say when it was, use the simple past: **I was in Italy in 2019**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Preguntas: **Have you ever been to…?** (¿has estado alguna vez…?). Respuestas: **Yes, I have.** / **No, I haven't.**",
     "@en": "Questions: **Have you ever been to…?** (have you ever been?). Responses: **Yes, I have.** / **No, I haven't.**"
    }
   ]
  },
